WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.479
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.779 --> 00:00:14.833
Unit eleven: Environmental Action. Today you will imagine a different past with the third conditional.

4
00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.902
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.436
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:24.528
Carbon footprint.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:29.293
Carbon footprint means the amount of carbon dioxide your actions produce.

8
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:32.138
Cycling lowers my carbon footprint.

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.646
Your turn. Say: Carbon footprint.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.780
Carbon footprint.

11
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:41.680
Zero waste.

12
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:45.252
Zero waste means producing no rubbish.

13
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.233
Our canteen is going zero waste.

14
00:00:48.817 --> 00:00:51.748
Your turn. Say: Zero waste.

15
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.961
Zero waste.

16
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:58.182
Renewable resource.

17
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:03.064
Renewable resource means something nature replaces, like sun or wind.

18
00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.650
Sunlight is a renewable resource.

19
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.460
Your turn. Say: Renewable resource.

20
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.696
Renewable resource.

21
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.532
Activism.

22
00:01:16.517 --> 00:01:19.433
Activism means taking action to cause change.

23
00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.862
Youth activism is growing around the world.

24
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.708
Your turn. Say: Activism.

25
00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:29.719
Activism.

26
00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:31.426
Petition.

27
00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:35.891
Petition means a document many people sign to ask for change.

28
00:01:36.483 --> 00:01:39.179
We signed a petition to ban plastic bags.

29
00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:42.575
Your turn. Say: Petition.

30
00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:46.272
Petition.

31
00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:48.668
Sustainability goal.

32
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:53.064
Sustainability goal means a target to protect the environment.

33
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.648
Our school's sustainability goal is zero plastic.

34
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.390
Your turn. Say: Sustainability goal.

35
00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:05.001
Sustainability goal.

36
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.088
Green initiative.

37
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:11.546
Green initiative means a new plan to help the environment.

38
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.440
The tree-planting day was a green initiative.

39
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.248
Your turn. Say: Green initiative.

40
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.345
Green initiative.

41
00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:24.363
Climate strike.

42
00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:28.859
Climate strike means a protest to demand action on climate.

43
00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.181
Students around the world joined a climate strike.

44
00:02:32.783 --> 00:02:35.714
Your turn. Say: Climate strike.

45
00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.928
Climate strike.

46
00:02:40.683 --> 00:02:42.079
Eco-conscious.

47
00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:45.814
Eco-conscious means caring about the environment.

48
00:02:46.417 --> 00:02:49.043
Eco-conscious shoppers bring their own bags.

49
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.535
Your turn. Say: Eco-conscious.

50
00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.807
Eco-conscious.

51
00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:58.841
Policy change.

52
00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:02.395
Policy change means a new official rule.

53
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:05.343
The petition led to a policy change.

54
00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.403
Your turn. Say: Policy change.

55
00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:13.825
Policy change.

56
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:15.654
Advocacy.

57
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.207
Advocacy means speaking up for a cause.

58
00:03:19.817 --> 00:03:21.781
Advocacy can change laws.

59
00:03:22.383 --> 00:03:25.407
Your turn. Say: Advocacy.

60
00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:29.256
Advocacy.

61
00:03:30.017 --> 00:03:30.925
Impact.

62
00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:33.986
Impact means a strong effect.

63
00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:36.641
Small actions have a big impact.

64
00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.566
Your turn. Say: Impact.

65
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:43.308
Impact.

66
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.937
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:48.783 --> 00:03:52.652
Visal, what environmental action would you like to take part in?

68
00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:58.910
A river clean-up. If we had started earlier, the river would have been cleaner.

69
00:04:00.017 --> 00:04:01.900
Have you signed any petitions?

70
00:04:03.017 --> 00:04:08.641
Yes, against plastic bags. It led to a policy change at our market!

71
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.448
What would have happened without it?

72
00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:16.105
If we hadn't spoken up, nothing would have changed.

73
00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.104
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.635
Grammar focus: Third conditional.

75
00:04:22.935 --> 00:04:24.191
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:24.883 --> 00:04:27.858
If we had acted sooner, the impact would have been smaller.

77
00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.702
If they had recycled, the river would have stayed clean.

78
00:04:32.617 --> 00:04:35.406
If I had known, I would have joined the strike.

79
00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:40.560
Use the third conditional for imagined past situations that did not happen.

80
00:04:41.317 --> 00:04:46.082
Be careful! Don't say: If we had acted sooner, the impact would be smaller.

81
00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:51.368
Say: If we had acted sooner, the impact would have been smaller.

82
00:04:51.668 --> 00:04:54.863
The third conditional uses 'would have' + past participle.

83
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:58.145
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:58.933 --> 00:05:00.074
Taking Action.

85
00:05:00.374 --> 00:05:04.184
Reducing my carbon footprint through zero waste habits makes an impact.

86
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.372
Our class started a petition to ban plastic straws.

87
00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.852
If we had acted sooner, less plastic would have reached the river.

88
00:05:13.867 --> 00:05:18.211
Youth activism and eco-conscious choices can lead to real policy change.

89
00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.906
Every green initiative brings us closer to our sustainability goal.

90
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.990
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:32.161
If we had acted sooner, the impact would have blank smaller.

92
00:05:32.461 --> 00:05:35.360
A, been. B, be. C, being.

93
00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.737
The answer is A: been.

94
00:05:41.883 --> 00:05:45.183
A document many people sign to ask for change is a blank.

95
00:05:45.483 --> 00:05:49.334
A, petition. B, policy. C, strike.

96
00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.074
The answer is A: petition.

97
00:05:56.217 --> 00:05:58.727
Caring about the environment is being blank.

98
00:05:59.027 --> 00:06:03.482
A, eco-conscious. B, renewable. C, zero waste.

99
00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.729
The answer is A: eco-conscious.

100
00:06:10.933 --> 00:06:14.294
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:18.334
What environmental action would you like to take part in?

102
00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.627
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:28.927 --> 00:06:37.826
I would like to join a tree-planting project. If people had planted more trees before, our city would have been cooler.

104
00:06:38.126 --> 00:06:39.858
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.703
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and third conditional.

106
00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:51.568
Today's value is environmental responsibility. Small green actions at home help the whole planet.

107
00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:54.381
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

108
00:06:54.681 --> 00:06:57.159
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

